{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","text":"DirectedHypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Positions ","type":"text"},{"code":"0 ..< P_s","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index order and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within one in ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"P_s + q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is target incidence ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in the same order. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, and of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessorIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inHyperedgeIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" plus n, or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"does not offer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"code":"IncidenceGraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"inEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/directedincidencegraphview"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs26DirectedIncidenceGraphViewV","modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift#L41","fileName":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift"}},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"t